  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AFRITACs and ATI - IMF umbrella agreement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The IMF promotes revenue mobilization in support of sustainable development, and it provides technical assistance for a select group of countries to achieve this. The expected outcomes are enhanced revenue performance, improved tax policy design, high-quality tax legislations and regulations, more effective tax administrations, more robust tax administration organizational structure, increased transparency, integrity, and accountability of the tax systems.

For the African Regional Technical Assistance Centres (AFRITACs), including African Training Institute (ATI), there is one joint result framework (same as for EU) that includes capacity development on public finance management, revenue administration, financial supervision and regulation, real sector macroeconomic statistics, real sector macro fiscal policies and inclusive growth and structural policies. The latter has specific goals related to climate change and gender. The logframe includes concrete objectives and outcome goals on gender equality. For instance that budget allocation systems and tools are in place for tracking and disclosing allocations for gender equality and women&#x2019;s empowerment.</narrative>
  </description>
